{"id":"mahabharata-12-284","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":284,"title":"चतुरशीत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 284 · The householder's dharma and austerity","summary":{"en":"Parashara ends the dharma of the householder and begins the teaching on austerity, which is open to all and shows the way to heaven to the self-controlled. He says that as all rivers reach the sea, so do all the other orders find their place in the householder's.","kn":"ಗೃಹಸ್ಥ ಧರ್ಮ ಮುಗಿಸಿ ಪರಾಶರ ತಪಸ್ಸಿನ ಬೋಧನೆ ಆರಂಭಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ತಪಸ್ಸು ಎಲ್ಲರಿಗೂ ತೆರೆದಿದೆ, ಜಿತೇಂದ್ರಿಯನಿಗೆ ಸ್ವರ್ಗ ಮಾರ್ಗ ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ನದಿಗಳೆಲ್ಲ ಸಮುದ್ರ ಸೇರುವಂತೆ ಇತರ ಆಶ್ರಮಗಳೆಲ್ಲ ಗೃಹಸ್ಥನಲ್ಲಿ ಆಶ್ರಯ ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"पराशर गृहस्थ धर्म समाप्त कर तप का उपदेश आरम्भ करते हैं जो सबके लिए खुला है और जितेन्द्रिय को स्वर्ग का मार्ग दिखाता है। वे कहते हैं कि जैसे सब नदियाँ समुद्र में जाती हैं वैसे सब आश्रम गृहस्थ में स्थान पाते हैं।","te":"పరాశరుడు గృహస్థ ధర్మాన్ని ముగించి తపస్సు బోధన ప్రారంభిస్తాడు; తపస్సు అందరికీ తెరిచి ఉంది, జితేంద్రియునికి స్వర్గ మార్గం చూపుతుంది. నదులన్నీ సముద్రం చేరినట్లు ఇతర ఆశ్రమాలన్నీ గృహస్థునిలో స్థానం పొందుతాయని అంటాడు.","ta":"இல்லற தர்மத்தை முடித்துப் பராசரர் தவப் போதனையைத் தொடங்குகிறார்; தவம் அனைவருக்கும் திறந்தது, புலனடக்கியவனுக்குச் சொர்க்க வழி காட்டுகிறது. ஆறுகள் எல்லாம் கடலை அடைவது போல் பிற ஆசிரமங்கள் இல்லறத்தில் இடம் பெறுகின்றன என்கிறார்.","ml":"ഗൃഹസ്ഥന്റെ ധർമ്മം അവസാനിപ്പിച്ച പരാശരൻ, എല്ലാവർക്കും തുറന്നിരിക്കുന്നതും ആത്മനിയന്ത്രണമുള്ളവർക്ക് സ്വർഗ്ഗത്തിലേക്കുള്ള വഴി കാണിക്കുന്നതുമായ തപസ്സിനെക്കുറിച്ചുള്ള ഉപദേശം തുടങ്ങുന്നു. എല്ലാ നദികളും കടലിലെത്തുന്നതുപോലെ, മറ്റെല്ലാ വർണ്ണങ്ങളും ഗൃഹസ്ഥന്റെ ആശ്രമത്തിൽ സ്ഥാനം കണ്ടെത്തുന്നുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.284; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"पराशर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Parashara said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एष धर्मविधिस्तात गृहस्थस्य प्रकीर्तितः ।\nतपोविधिं तु वक्ष्यामि तन्मे निगदतः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear one, this is the rule of dharma declared for the householder. Now I will tell the rule of austerity; listen to me as I speak."}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रायेण हि गृहस्थस्य ममत्वं नाम जायते ।\nसङ्गागतं नरश्रेष्ठ भावैस्तामसराजसैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the householder, a sense of \"mine\" usually arises, born of attachment, through states of dullness and passion."}},{"n":3,"text":"गृहाण्याश्रित्य गावश्च क्षेत्राणि च धनानि च ।\nदाराः पुत्राश्च भृत्याश्च भवन्तीह नरस्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Resting on houses, cattle, fields and wealth, wives, sons and servants come to a man here."}},{"n":4,"text":"एवं तस्य प्रवृत्तस्य नित्यमेवानुपश्यतः ।\nरागद्वेषौ विवर्धेते ह्यनित्यत्वमपश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he goes on in this way, always looking at these things and not seeing impermanence, his desire and hatred grow."}},{"n":5,"text":"रागद्वेषाभिभूतं च नरं द्रव्यवशानुगम् ।\nमोहजाता रतिर्नाम समुपैति नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a man is overcome by desire and hatred and follows the pull of possessions, a pleasure born of delusion, called attachment to enjoyment, comes to him, lord of men."}},{"n":6,"text":"कृतार्थो भोगतो भूत्वा स वै रतिपरायणः ।\nलाभं ग्राम्यसुखादन्यं रतितो नानुपश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gained his ends through enjoyment, he becomes devoted to pleasure and sees no gain other than the worldly pleasure of enjoyment."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततो लोभाभिभूतात्मा सङ्गाद्वर्धयते जनम् ।\nपुष्ट्यर्थं चैव तस्येह जनस्यार्थं चिकीर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with a self overcome by greed, he increases his dependents out of attachment, and seeks wealth for the support of those people."}},{"n":8,"text":"स जानन्नपि चाकार्यमर्थार्थं सेवते नरः ।\nबालस्नेहपरीतात्मा तत्क्षयाच्चानुतप्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even knowing what should not be done, that man does it for the sake of wealth; his mind full of tender affection for his children, he grieves when they decline."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो मानेन संपन्नो रक्षन्नात्मपराजयम् ।\nकरोति येन भोगी स्यामिति तस्माद्विनश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, filled with pride and guarding against his own defeat, he does whatever will make him an enjoyer, and so he is ruined."}},{"n":10,"text":"तपो हि बुद्धियुक्तानां शाश्वतं ब्रह्मदर्शनम् ।\nअन्विच्छतां शुभं कर्म नराणां त्यजतां सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Austerity is the lasting vision of Brahman for those endowed with understanding, for men who seek good action and give up pleasure."}},{"n":11,"text":"स्नेहायतननाशाच्च धननाशाच्च पार्थिव ।\nआधिव्याधिप्रतापाच्च निर्वेदमुपगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through the loss of what he loves, the loss of wealth, and the torment of mental and bodily illness, a man comes to disenchantment, king."}},{"n":12,"text":"निर्वेदादात्मसंबोधः संबोधाच्छास्त्रदर्शनम् ।\nशास्त्रार्थदर्शनाद्राजंस्तप एवानुपश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"From disenchantment comes knowledge of the self; from that knowledge, insight into the scriptures; and from seeing the meaning of the scriptures, he sees that austerity alone is the way."}},{"n":13,"text":"दुर्लभो हि मनुष्येन्द्र नरः प्रत्यवमर्शवान् ।\nयो वै प्रियसुखे क्षीणे तपः कर्तुं व्यवस्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who reflects, lord of men, is rare: one who, when his dear pleasures have wasted away, resolves to practice austerity."}},{"n":14,"text":"तपः सर्वगतं तात हीनस्यापि विधीयते ।\nजितेन्द्रियस्य दान्तस्य स्वर्गमार्गप्रदेशकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Austerity, dear one, is available to all, even to the lowly; for one of subdued senses and self-control it points the road to heaven."}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रजापतिः प्रजाः पूर्वमसृजत्तपसा विभुः ।\nक्वचित्क्वचिद्व्रतपरो व्रतान्यास्थाय पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago the lord Prajapati created creatures through austerity, devoted to vows here and there, having undertaken vows, king."}},{"n":16,"text":"आदित्या वसवो रुद्रास्तथैवाग्न्यश्विमारुताः ।\nविश्वेदेवास्तथा साध्याः पितरोऽथ मरुद्गणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Adityas, Vasus and Rudras, likewise Agni, the Ashvins and the Maruts, the Vishvedevas, the Sadhyas, the ancestors and the hosts of Maruts,"}},{"n":17,"text":"यक्षराक्षसगन्धर्वाः सिद्धाश्चान्ये दिवौकसः ।\nसंसिद्धास्तपसा तात ये चान्ये स्वर्गवासिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Yakshas, Rakshasas and Gandharvas, the Siddhas and the other dwellers in the sky, dear one, and the others who live in heaven were perfected by austerity."}},{"n":18,"text":"ये चादौ ब्रह्मणा सृष्टा ब्राह्मणास्तपसा पुरा ।\nते भावयन्तः पृथिवीं विचरन्ति दिवं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the Brahmins, who were created long ago by Brahma through austerity, move about the earth and heaven nourishing them."}},{"n":19,"text":"मर्त्यलोके च राजानो ये चान्ये गृहमेधिनः ।\nमहाकुलेषु दृश्यन्ते तत्सर्वं तपसः फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings in the world of mortals and other householders seen in great families: all that is the fruit of austerity."}},{"n":20,"text":"कौशिकानि च वस्त्राणि शुभान्याभरणानि च ।\nवाहनासनयानानि सर्वं तत्तपसः फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Silken garments, fine ornaments, vehicles, seats and carriages: all that is the fruit of austerity."}},{"n":21,"text":"मनोनुकूलाः प्रमदा रूपवत्यः सहस्रशः ।\nवासः प्रासादपृष्ठे च तत्सर्वं तपसः फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Women agreeable to the mind, beautiful, in thousands, and a dwelling on the roof of a palace: all that is the fruit of austerity."}},{"n":22,"text":"शयनानि च मुख्यानि भोज्यानि विविधानि च ।\nअभिप्रेतानि सर्वाणि भवन्ति कृतकर्मणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Excellent beds and various foods, whatever they wish, come to those who have done the work."}},{"n":23,"text":"नाप्राप्यं तपसा किंचित्त्रैलोक्येऽस्मिन्परंतप ।\nउपभोगपरित्यागः फलान्यकृतकर्मणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nothing in these three worlds is out of reach of austerity, scorcher of foes; but giving up enjoyment is the fruit of those who have not done the work."}},{"n":24,"text":"सुखितो दुःखितो वापि नरो लोभं परित्यजेत् ।\nअवेक्ष्य मनसा शास्त्रं बुद्ध्या च नृपसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man, happy or unhappy, should give up greed, considering the scriptures with his mind and understanding, best of kings."}},{"n":25,"text":"असंतोषोऽसुखायैव लोभादिन्द्रियविभ्रमः ।\nततोऽस्य नश्यति प्रज्ञा विद्येवाभ्यासवर्जिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Discontent leads only to unhappiness; from greed comes the confusion of the senses; and then his wisdom perishes, like learning left unpracticed."}},{"n":26,"text":"नष्टप्रज्ञो यदा भवति तदा न्यायं न पश्यति ।\nतस्मात्सुखक्षये प्राप्ते पुमानुग्रं तपश्चरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he has lost his wisdom, he no longer sees what is right. So when happiness is exhausted, a man should practice fierce austerity."}},{"n":27,"text":"यदिष्टं तत्सुखं प्राहुर्द्वेष्यं दुःखमिहोच्यते ।\nकृताकृतस्य तपसः फलं पश्यस्व यादृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is desired they call happiness, and what is hated is called suffering here. See what kind of fruit follows austerity done or not done."}},{"n":28,"text":"नित्यं भद्राणि पश्यन्ति विषयांश्चोपभुञ्जते ।\nप्राकाश्यं चैव गच्छन्ति कृत्वा निष्कल्मषं तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who have done austerity free of stain always see good things, enjoy the objects of the senses, and come to renown."}},{"n":29,"text":"अप्रियाण्यवमानांश्च दुःखं बहुविधात्मकम् ।\nफलार्थी सत्पथत्यक्तः प्राप्नोति विषयात्मकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The seeker of fruit who has left the right path meets with disagreeable things, insults and suffering of many kinds, which belong to the objects of sense."}},{"n":30,"text":"धर्मे तपसि दाने च विचिकित्सास्य जायते ।\nस कृत्वा पापकान्येव निरयं प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who has doubt about dharma, austerity and giving, having done only evil, goes to hell."}},{"n":31,"text":"सुखे तु वर्तमानो वै दुःखे वापि नरोत्तम ।\nस्ववृत्ताद्यो न चलति शास्त्रचक्षुः स मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the man, best of men, who in happiness or in suffering does not budge from his own course, and whose eye is the scripture, is truly a man."}},{"n":32,"text":"इषुप्रपातमात्रं हि स्पर्शयोगे रतिः स्मृता ।\nरसने दर्शने घ्राणे श्रवणे च विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The pleasure in contact is held to last only as long as an arrow's flight, and so too in taste, sight, smell and hearing, lord of the people."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततोऽस्य जायते तीव्रा वेदना तत्क्षयात्पुनः ।\nबुधा येन प्रशंसन्ति मोक्षं सुखमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then sharp pain arises in him when it ends, and by that the wise praise liberation as the highest happiness."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततः फलार्थं चरति भवन्ति ज्यायसो गुणाः ।\nधर्मवृत्त्या च सततं कामार्थाभ्यां न हीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he acts for the sake of the fruit, and his good qualities grow greater; by living in dharma he is never cut off from desire and wealth."}},{"n":35,"text":"अप्रयत्नागताः सेव्या गृहस्थैर्विषयाः सदा ।\nप्रयत्नेनोपगम्यश्च स्वधर्म इति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Householders should always enjoy the objects that come without effort, and one should approach them with effort as one's own dharma, so I think."}},{"n":36,"text":"मानिनां कुलजातानां नित्यं शास्त्रार्थचक्षुषाम् ।\nधर्मक्रियावियुक्तानामशक्त्या संवृतात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the proud, born in good families, always with the scriptures as their eyes, who are without dharma's rites and cannot perform them and are restrained in themselves,"}},{"n":37,"text":"क्रियमाणं यदा कर्म नाशं गच्छति मानुषम् ।\nतेषां नान्यदृते लोके तपसः कर्म विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"when the action they perform is lost to man, nothing else in the world remains for them but the action of austerity."}},{"n":38,"text":"सर्वात्मना तु कुर्वीत गृहस्थः कर्मनिश्चयम् ।\nदाक्ष्येण हव्यकव्यार्थं स्वधर्मं विचरेन्नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the householder should do his work with firm resolve and his whole self, and should carry out his own dharma with skill for the sake of offerings to gods and ancestors, king."}},{"n":39,"text":"यथा नदीनदाः सर्वे सागरे यान्ति संस्थितिम् ।\nएवमाश्रमिणः सर्वे गृहस्थे यान्ति संस्थितिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As all rivers and streams find their rest in the ocean, so all those in the orders of life find their rest in the householder."}}]}]}